; Only two directories exist as far as dune is concerned. Everything else in the
; repository -- `crates/`, `xtask/`, `fuzz/`, `target/`, `docs/` -- is invisible,
; so `dune build` never walks the Cargo output and never sees a stray `dune` file.
(dirs engines spec)

; `spec/` holds data and no build rules. Marking it data-only stops dune from
; looking for `dune` files inside it while keeping every file available as a
; dependency of a rule.
(data_only_dirs spec)
